# Strict Coding Rules

Mandatory for all code. Violations block commit via `scripts/check-quality.sh`.

## TypeScript / React / Next.js

- `strict` mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`
- Validate every external boundary (forms, route handlers, server actions, env) with Zod or equivalent
- Functions ≤ 25 lines; files ≤ 300 target / 400 hard max
- Parameters ≤ 3 — options object when more
- Imports at top of file — no inline imports
- Every `catch` handles or reports with context — no silent swallowing
- No `console.*` in production code
- No raw `fetch`/`axios` scattered in UI — go through one project API module
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only where interactivity requires it
- Next.js in this repo has breaking changes vs. training data — read
  `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using an API

## Security

- Secrets in env — never committed; only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` reaches the client
- Never trust client input in server actions / route handlers
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with unsanitized content

## Testing

See `testing-standards.mdc`. Tests are mandatory for behavior changes — not optional follow-up.
